  "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{7}(0+4) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{12}{7} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{12}{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the intersection points are\n $(\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{7}},0)$ and $(-\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{7}},0).$",
